{"id": "1549224461448781906", "channel_id": "1544152565921611837", "author_id": "310254141639491590", "author_name": "alexisvaunt", "content": "I feel like everything's kind of been said already, but I want to add my own thoughts. If the idea is to have the difficulty scale up by wave as well as by difficulty, you need to make it so the rewards are designed for that. As it stands, new players *cannot* complete Normal, and knowing all of the rewards that are locked behind that when previously those rewards would be available for the much-more-possible a1/a2 clears is extremely discouraging. I get that this is to incentivize new players to spend money to strengthen characters, but I'm going to be really real here, it doesn't do that. It just makes me not want to play D-tide, which means I'm just going to quit once I finish the story because the endgame is unavailable for me. The worst part, I think, is that I was intending to spend to support a game with a dev team that seemed to *care*, but now even if the changes are rolled back (which they won't be, I know that), I don't see myself spending any money on this game for the foreseeable future. It feels awful.\n\nIf your goal was to sabotage yourselves, I think you did an *excellent* job of it. If not, maybe consider listening to the community this time.", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T01:04:54.808000+00:00", "thread_id": "1544152565921611837", "reactions": [{"emoji": "🤣", "emoji_id": null, "count": 1}], "thread_title": "D-tide Feedback (New)", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542479601241030726"]}
